---
source: crates/togi/tests/read/events.rs
expression: text(&ran.stdout)
---
Print the journal, one readable line per event

Oldest first. Filters combine, so you can narrow the journal to one core, one trial or a time window. A different ruleset warns before rendering, including `--json`; a different schema is refused. An event of a kind this build does not know is skipped and an unknown field is ignored, `--json` included; stderr says which, after the output. A kind selector must name a known exact kind or group; an unknown name and an explicitly empty list are usage errors (exit 2). A valid filter with no matches prints nothing and exits 0. Readable lines are colored on terminals and in the system journal unless `NO_COLOR` is set.

Usage: togi events [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --core <N>
          Only events naming core N, and the outcomes of trials that load it

      --state-dir <path>
          State directory
          
          [default: /var/lib/togi]

      --kind <kinds>
          Only these comma-separated known kinds, or groups such as trial for every trial.* kind
          
          [possible values: backend, backend.retry, boot, boot.leave_reason, boot.saved_entry, checking, checking.chain, checking.cycle, checking.step, combination, command, command.reset, config, config.loaded, core, core.phase, crash, crash.detected, day, day.answer, day.boot_start, day.checkpoint, day.clean_stop, day.fault, day.offsets_changed, day.unclean_end, deadend, deepening, deepening.round, defect, defect.answered, defect.found, failure, failure.carried, host, host.ranking, hunt, hunt.end, hunt.group, hunt.skipped, hunt.start, journal, journal.torn, mce, preflight, preflight.check, profile, profile.applied, profile.change, profile.restored, session, session.archived, session.baseline, session.carried, session.context, session.notice, session.start, session.warning, shutdown, smu, smu.error, smu.intent, smu.readback, smu.write, state, state.rebuilt, trial, trial.carried, trial.end, trial.intent, trial.progress, trial.sample, trial.signal, trial.start, tuner, tuner.decision, tuner.warning]

      --trial <ID>
          Only events of trial ID

      --since <time>
          Only events at or after this RFC 3339 time

      --until <time>
          Only events before this RFC 3339 time

      --json
          Print raw, uncolored JSON events

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
  togi events --core 3                      Everything that happened to core 3
  togi events --kind trial,checking.cycle   Every trial event and checking cycle
  togi events --json --trial 0413           The raw events of trial 0413
